WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.900
Safety, security, and governance.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.669
Regulated industries pay a premium for engineers who speak this fluently.

3
00:00:07.669 --> 00:00:09.567
Here are the first seven terms.

4
00:00:10.767 --> 00:00:15.933
Prompt injection is the number one unsolved security problem of LLM apps.

5
00:00:16.233 --> 00:00:20.467
Direct injection is when the user's input overrides your instructions.

6
00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:30.667
Indirect injection hides malicious instructions in content the system processes, like a retrieved document, a webpage, or an email your agent reads.

7
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:33.367
So assume all retrieved text is hostile.

8
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:38.933
Jailbreaking means crafting inputs that bypass a model's safety training.

9
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.800
Common tricks include roleplay framing, encoding tricks, and many-shot attacks.

10
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.418
The defense is depth.

11
00:00:45.418 --> 00:00:47.300
Never rely on the model alone.

12
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.267
System-prompt hardening means writing prompts that survive attack.

13
00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.200
Set clear precedence rules.

14
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.300
Include refusal instructions.

15
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.067
Put delimiters around untrusted content.

16
00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.467
And never put secrets in the prompt, because it can be leaked.

17
00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:07.767
Guardrails are programmatic input and output checks around the model.

18
00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.533
At the center is the probabilistic model.

19
00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:18.233
Around it sits a deterministic shell: topic filters, PII scrubbing, schema validation, and toxicity screens.

20
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:21.167
These are the guardrail toolkits.

21
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:24.833
NVIDIA NeMo uses dialog rails written in Colang.

22
00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:27.567
Guardrails AI offers a validator hub.

23
00:01:27.867 --> 00:01:31.167
LLM Guard provides input and output scanners.

24
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:35.567
And Lakera is managed injection detection, of Gandalf game fame.

25
00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:41.633
Red teaming means systematically attacking your own system before adversaries do.

26
00:01:41.933 --> 00:01:45.733
You try injections, jailbreaks, and data extraction attempts.

27
00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:51.100
The deliverable is a findings report, plus a regression test for every hole you found.

28
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.567
PII detection finds and masks personal data.

29
00:01:55.867 --> 00:02:01.333
That means names, phone numbers, and IDs like Aadhaar or social security numbers.

30
00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:05.169
It happens before the data reaches the model or the logs.

31
00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:11.000
Presidio is the standard open source tool, and it is a hard requirement in fintech and health.

32
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.022
Let's recap.

33
00:02:13.022 --> 00:02:18.300
Prompt injection is the biggest unsolved problem, so trust no retrieved text.

34
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.633
Harden prompts, but layer guardrails around the model.

35
00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:24.667
Red team your system and keep regression tests.

36
00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:28.733
And mask personal data before it reaches the model or the logs.
